{"skill":{"slug":"stock-analysis","displayName":"Stock Analysis"},"version":{"version":"6.2.0","createdAt":1770041353575,"changelog":"🔮 Rumor Scanner: M&A rumors, insider activity, Twitter whispers, impact scoring","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"App-Plan.md","size":14708,"sha256":"98276ba3eb8d91373827e7941abf66e3b1affb684fc8dc758721ba49d50d9f31","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":6390,"sha256":"899b51e9272962824c9f789f493224410fed6b87f2df7dbdf3f05d0d1edc617c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8230,"sha256":"6ae566bdf7f099f0926c58966a5d9d11531c366264217237de281387bf47964d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"TODO.md","size":12848,"sha256":"3e3cc7022797587ee8298e1a0503bebf4a3494c9ebda15a9f951799a7b310682","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","size":16594,"sha256":"b2a86717592fd7f719cbc1022711cd03af4f5dcfd709c738d049f7c0de0b3856","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"docs/CONCEPT.md","size":9101,"sha256":"3df36f8710cb6e64d3f0bc3c091b1c70e7eac979ba352f46fa4ac09b865c5517","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"docs/HOT_SCANNER.md","size":5865,"sha256":"0c42df93f631b30f834d3eff27805650965b62afdf855e7e40d950415dc2666b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"docs/README.md","size":2405,"sha256":"86c36fdce36c7c9ebb52f70966b16bdfe17016a54a4861932fc01d4b8c711912","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"docs/USAGE.md","size":8898,"sha256":"9cc1aada593ae985ea755003eafed3a8f564f1af77853501c89ac48439cf9174","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/analyze_stock.py","size":89930,"sha256":"24e05932926903ccee7e8fb5c621da5d354ae01857a020e26e77bdcb37df345a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/dividends.py","size":13130,"sha256":"f7345eda9b5eb164502cd770fedf6230bdc9eaabc2d949d9b48b1ab02d4f4169","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/hot_scanner.py","size":24620,"sha256":"9a0f9d57a2cc919b351e210072a061b58deaca47294b0ce67dc5bbb7839741f5","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/portfolio.py","size":18897,"sha256":"2ef732f6c0a0a9bff4ed016d75007c44d2ddd43a52bd5e25ca8716a56355523a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/rumor_scanner.py","size":11578,"sha256":"315360567ac98f7edae0c9e448360ee4bdecfe3463b07954481a95c17c12dd5a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/test_stock_analysis.py","size":11958,"sha256":"2fe52876bdc2aa5f8dda67a7230b3b798ebdb0ccbc426c9aa959237310fe255c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/watchlist.py","size":11542,"sha256":"342730d649fb27e3a179adebd8842b236658c4cf706cccf32e42c3c133c42dac","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2547,"sha256":"8850685afe8350661127a3d9b790716c5a1444d2caebf0fea5f91f2a1a0cbdf6","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015754220,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9e6becd9fbc3b54c3616f450a56cfdcfd1f067a38e29c0cce0afad437887311d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9e6becd9fbc3b54c3616f450a56cfdcfd1f067a38e29c0cce0afad437887311d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: stock-analysis\nVersion: 6.2.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its reliance on an external, user-installed `bird` CLI tool for Twitter/X integration, as detailed in `SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `scripts/hot_scanner.py`, and `scripts/rumor_scanner.py`. This external dependency introduces a supply chain risk, as the security of the skill becomes dependent on the security of the `bird` binary. Furthermore, the skill instructs users to manually extract sensitive `AUTH_TOKEN` and `CT0` session cookies from their browser and store them in a `.env` file, which are then loaded by the Python scripts and passed to the `bird` CLI. While the skill's own code does not appear to intentionally exfiltrate these credentials, this practice exposes sensitive user session tokens to an external binary, significantly increasing the attack surface and potential for unauthorized access if the `bird` CLI or the user's environment is compromised.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159738721},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":20,"checkedAt":1789015754220},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This stock-analysis skill is mostly coherent, but its optional X/Twitter scanning asks users to expose live session credentials to a third-party CLI with overly broad environment access.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Hot Scanner and Rumor Scanner load every key from a project .env into the process environment and pass a full os.environ copy to Bird; only the X credentials appear needed for that integration.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The manifest only declares uv, while the documented social feature requires an unpinned globally installed @steipete/bird CLI and open-ended Python dependency versions, so the effective executed code can change after review.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill documents network data collection, local portfolio/watchlist storage, optional cron use, and X/Twitter credential setup, but it under-discloses the sensitivity of AUTH_TOKEN/CT0 cookies, Full Disk Access guidance, and full environment forwarding to Bird.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Portfolio and watchlist persistence to ~/.clawdbot/skills/stock-analysis and cache files under the skill directory are expected for the feature set and partly disclosed, but users should treat holdings, cost basis, alerts, and scan caches as sensitive local financial data.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Core stock, crypto, portfolio, watchlist, dividend, news, and trend analysis capabilities fit the stated purpose, but X/Twitter rumor scanning relies on browser/session credentials and a third-party executable in a way that is high-impact for a finance skill.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review carefully before installing. The core stock and portfolio features are understandable, but avoid enabling the X/Twitter features unless you are comfortable giving a third-party CLI access to live session cookies. Do not place unrelated secrets in the skill .env or run it from a shell containing sensitive environment variables, and treat saved portfolio/watchlist files as private financial data.","findings":"[AST4] expected: Calling Bird as a subprocess is consistent with the documented X/Twitter search feature, but the global executable trust boundary and inherited environment make it a review concern rather than a standalone malicious finding.\n[LP3] unexpected: The metadata understates the documented runtime authority: network access, local file writes, subprocess execution, and optional credential use are present but not declared in the manifest requirements.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The X/Twitter integration is related to trend and rumor detection, but instructions to use browser cookies, environment variables, and Full Disk Access are broader and riskier than the stock-analysis purpose requires.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: The guide explicitly normalizes extracting live X/Twitter session cookies and does not provide adequate warnings or safer scoped authentication guidance.\n[SQP-2] expected: Portfolio/watchlist storage and external ticker lookups are expected for finance tracking, but the skill should more clearly warn that holdings, quantities, cost basis, and tickers may reveal sensitive financial information.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The product analytics roadmap is not active runtime behavior in the inspected skill, so it does not drive the verdict, but it would need privacy controls if implemented.\n[SQP-1] expected: The description is broad, but the advertised commands are finance-related and coherent with the skill; this is a minor routing risk, not a primary concern.\n[E2] unexpected: The scanners forward the complete environment to Bird after loading .env values; passing unrelated secrets is not necessary for the documented social search function.\n[PE3] unexpected: Reading a .env file for AUTH_TOKEN and CT0 is expected only for optional X/Twitter auth, but importing every variable globally is overbroad.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding is supported by artifact code: both hot_scanner.py and rumor_scanner.py combine broad .env loading with full-environment subprocess execution.\n[T08] unexpected: The supply-chain finding is supported as a review concern because Bird is installed globally without a pinned version and Python dependencies use lower-bound-only constraints; no active dependency compromise was found.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015754220}}}}}